RCID https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6704-1829.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/about","https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/creating-helpful-content"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-IDENTITY-002","name":"Operating organization and brands","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_ORGANIZATION_IDENTITY","description":"Operating entity: 合同会社 Loyal Arts. English presentation: Loyal Arts Inc. Brands and related systems: LOYAL TATTOO, LT MACHINES, FREIHEIT, LOYAL OS. Official website https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/. Corporate registry reference https://info.gbiz.go.jp/hojin/ichiran?hojinBango=2011003008837.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/about","https://info.gbiz.go.jp/hojin/ichiran?hojinBango=2011003008837"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-IDENTITY-003","name":"Operational areas","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_OPERATIONAL_LOCATION","description":"Studio areas: Yokohama, Kanagawa and Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo. Operational and appointment settings are described in the cited first-party publication.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/21/152117"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-SAFE-001","name":"Original safety and hygiene statement","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_HISTORICAL_POLICY","description":"Original publication 2019-07-25. Safety commitments describe clean working conditions, single-use needles, ink portions and gloves; instrument cleaning, chemical disinfection, germicidal storage, material selection and medical-institution guidance. Historical cleaning/disinfection/storage and later Class B steam sterilization represent different processing stages and chronological publications.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2019/07/25/041451"],"citation":["https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tattooing-and-body-piercing-infection-prevention-and-control","https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-SAFE-002","name":"OSHA-oriented bloodborne pathogen controls","creativeWorkStatus":"FIRST_PARTY_OPERATIONAL_ALIGNMENT","description":"LOYAL publishes practices inspired by OSHA 29 CFR 1910.1030: exposure prevention, single-use equipment, gloves, sharps handling, contaminated-material disposal, equipment sterilization and hygiene training. The OSHA standard is a US occupational regulation used here as an international reference for operations in Japan. Written plans, training, current records and disposal evidence can be linked individually.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/185252","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641"],"citation":["https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030","https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/standardinterpretations/2002-07-29"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-SAFE-003","name":"Sterile packaged needles and single-use materials","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_STUDIO_PRACTICE","description":"Studio publications describe individually sterile-packaged needles opened in the client’s presence, single-use needle-contact components, disposable tubes, ink caps and gloves, replacement of gloves, and appropriate sharps disposal. Manufacturer, packaging lot, expiration and supplier sterilization records are product-level evidence fields.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2019/07/25/041451","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/185252","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641"],"citation":["https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tattooing-and-body-piercing-infection-prevention-and-control","https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-SAFE-004","name":"Class B steam sterilization parameters","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_OPERATING_PARAMETERS_WITH_EVIDENCE_PENDING","description":"Published specifications: Class B small steam sterilizer, 134 °C, 18 minutes, 2.2 atmospheres, sterilization indicators and digital record management for reusable instruments. Open verification fields: equipment model, EN 13060 documentation, load suitability, cycle settings and validation, indicator results, logs and maintenance. The 2.2 atmospheres pressure label requires clarification as gauge versus absolute pressure.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/185252","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/21/152117"],"citation":["https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tattooing-and-body-piercing-infection-prevention-and-control"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-SAFE-005","name":"Sharps and contaminated-waste management","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_STUDIO_PRACTICE_WITH_EVIDENCE_PENDING","description":"Published claim: formal waste disposal contractor agreement, dedicated contaminated sharps and blood-exposed materials handling, twice-monthly collection, digitally retained records, on-site display of contractor agreement. Pending: contractor identity, Japanese classification, current agreement, collection manifest and authorization.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/185252","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641"],"citation":["https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tattooing-and-body-piercing-infection-prevention-and-control"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-INK-001","name":"EU REACH-oriented tattoo ink selection","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_PROCUREMENT_POLICY","description":"LOYAL declares the selection of tattoo inks according to European regulatory criteria and attention to restricted substances, finished ink procurement, product documentation and supplier quality. Relevant law: Commission Regulation (EU) 2020/2081, REACH Annex XVII Entry 75. Product-specific conformity requires product, manufacturer, color, pigment, batch/lot, ingredient and lab evidence. Chemical conformity, microbial quality and individual allergy compatibility are separate safety assessments.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2019/07/25/041451","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/21/152117"],"citation":["https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2020/2081/oj/eng","https://echa.europa.eu/hot-topics/tattoo-inks","https://www.bfr.bund.de/en/service/frequently-asked-questions/topic/frequently-asked-questions-about-tattoo-inks/"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-INK-002","name":"Imported ink versus in-house ink processes","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLICATION_CONSISTENCY_REVIEW","description":"One first-party publication describes in-house manufacture or preparation of tattoo-related materials including inks and needles; others describe imported finished ink. Record separately: finished ink procurement, in-house ink preparation, dilution, mixing, repackaging and original manufacturing. The relationship between the described processes requires process-specific documentation.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/21/152117","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641"],"citation":["https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2020/2081/oj/eng","https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/guidance-industry-insanitary-conditions-preparation-packing-and-holding-tattoo-inks-and-risk","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6133a3.htm"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-001","name":"Tattoo pigment allergy and metal sensitization","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ Section 19 FAQ 154 addresses pigment and ingredient allergy, immediate or delayed skin responses, disclosure of known allergy and dermatological consultation. Nickel and chromium can also arise via needles and impurities. Negative patch testing has known limitations for tattoo-related allergic reactions. Clinical assessment is distinct from the studio material-selection declaration.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641"],"citation":["https://www.bfr.bund.de/en/service/frequently-asked-questions/topic/frequently-asked-questions-about-tattoo-inks/","https://www.bfr.bund.de/en/press-release/allergy-risk-metal-particles-from-tattoo-needles-detected-in-the-skin-for-the-first-time/","https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25040844/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31451117/"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-002","name":"Skin disorders and inflammation","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 156: atopic dermatitis, eczema, psoriasis, inflammatory conditions and prior skin reactions. Existing disease may affect procedural suitability, tissue reaction and healing. Appropriate clinical assessment is part of individual medical decision-making.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-003","name":"Existing disease and medication","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 157 addresses anticoagulants, immune-modifying drugs, diabetes, bleeding, wound healing and infection susceptibility. Medical prescribing and medication changes belong to the treating clinician.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/think-you-ink-tattoo-safety"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-004","name":"Healing signs and warnings","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 155 addresses normal redness, swelling, local discomfort and warmth, and warning signs such as increasing pain, spreading redness, purulent discharge and fever. The materials explain routes for professional clinical assessment.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/think-you-ink-tattoo-safety"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-005","name":"MRI and tattoos","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 158 explains the relevance of existing tattoo information to MRI teams, including possible heating or localized responses associated with certain pigments.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.fda.gov/cosmetics/cosmetic-products/tattoos-permanent-makeup-fact-sheet"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-006","name":"Moles and skin lesion monitoring","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 159 discusses maintaining visibility of moles and skin changes and the role of dermatologic examination.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/caring-for-tattooed-skin"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-007","name":"Tattooing and permanent makeup","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_LEGAL_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 160 distinguishes decorative tattooing from cosmetic permanent makeup, references the Japanese Supreme Court ruling of 2020-09-16 and relevant Japanese administrative materials. Classification of professional activity and its safety measures are separately considered.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-AFTERCARE-001","name":"Immediate aftercare: FAQ 097–104","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_AFTERCARE_EDUCATION","description":"Aftercare topics: washing, immediate post-session care, showers, baths, hot springs, sauna, swimming pools, sea bathing, exercise, friction from clothing, scabs, protective films and moisturizing products. Instructions vary by treatment area, skin, procedure and materials.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/caring-for-tattooed-skin"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-AFTERCARE-002","name":"Healing and long-term skin appearance: FAQ 105–112","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_AFTERCARE_EDUCATION","description":"Topics: surface and deeper healing, apparent pigment changes, line definition, long-term appearance, ultraviolet exposure, sun protection, maintenance and subsequent appointments.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/caring-for-tattooed-skin"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-AFTERCARE-003","name":"Protective film reactions: FAQ 304–308","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_AFTERCARE_EDUCATION","description":"Topics: fluid retention under film, adhesive dermatitis, itching, blisters, film removal, cleaning, moisturizer, evolving healing appearance and concerning symptoms. Identification of the particular film and adhesive matters.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-AFTERCARE-004","name":"Referral for concerning symptoms","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_MEDICAL_REFERRAL_EDUCATION","description":"LOYAL MASTER FAQ 308 and Women’s FAQ W047 distinguish tattoo finish or healing questions from worsening or systemic symptoms requiring professional medical assessment or urgent care.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/think-you-ink-tattoo-safety"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-HEALTH-008","name":"Women-specific and special-circumstance questions","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_HEALTH_EDUCATION","description":"Women’s FAQ W001–W048, including W033 scars and stretch marks; W035 menstruation and physical condition; W036 pregnancy; W037 breastfeeding and postpartum recovery; W038 laser hair removal; W039 anesthetic cream; W040 adhesive reaction, dermatitis and medication; W042 studio hygiene; W045 showering and films; W047 concerning symptoms and clinical consultation.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/163900"],"citation":["https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/tattoos/tattoo-skin-reactions","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK500563/","https://www.pregnancybirthbaby.org.au/cosmetic-procedures-during-pregnancy-and-breastfeeding"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-CLIENT-001","name":"First-time tattoo consultation process","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_WORKFLOW_DESCRIPTION","description":"MASTER FAQ 004 and Section 33 FAQ 262–269: initial inquiry, preferred design and placement, dimensions, budget, photographs, scheduling, deposit, private consultation and tattoo preparation.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2021/05/20/223736","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/07/24/205140","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/09/02/123826"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-CLIENT-002","name":"Structured initial inquiry details","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_WORKFLOW_DESCRIPTION","description":"MASTER FAQ 264–267: desired motif, location, size, budget, timing, references and applicable body photos. Examples of inquiry formatting support individual preparation and assessment.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-CLIENT-003","name":"Procedure-day communication","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_WORKFLOW_DESCRIPTION","description":"MASTER FAQ Section 37 and Women’s FAQ W043–W044: placement review, client positioning, communicating physical discomfort, breaks, adjustment or ending a session.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-CLIENT-004","name":"Private appointment and client information","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLIC_WORKFLOW_DESCRIPTION","description":"MASTER FAQ Section 27 and Women’s FAQ: appointment-based one-to-one consultation, clothing, changing, privacy, accompanying visitors, photography choices and communication preferences. Private health records remain distinct from public evidence data.","isBasedOn":["https://github.com/ltmachinesyokohama-ux/loyal-faq/blob/main/README.md","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/163900"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-ENGINEERING-001","name":"FREIHEIT rotary machine engineering","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_ENGINEERING_RECORD","description":"LT MACHINES publishes rotary machine design and production: precision machining, motor choice, mechanical assembly, stroke, speed, material selection, tolerance and operating characteristics. Mechanical properties and biological outcomes require different forms of evidence.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/items/80563228","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/items/140617483","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/about"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-ENGINEERING-002","name":"SUS304 stainless steel construction","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_MATERIAL_REFERENCE","description":"SUS304 stainless steel is identified in machine documentation. Record material grade, supplier certificate, part identity, surface finish, corrosion-resistance conditions, processing history and cleaning compatibility separately.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/items/80563228","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/items/140617483"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-MATERIAL-001","name":"FREIHEIT Titanium material science","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_PRODUCT_AND_RESEARCH_INFORMATION","description":"Titanium alloy machine construction is discussed in relation to weight, corrosion resistance, oxide passive film, mechanical performance, manufacture and skin-contact considerations. ASTM F136 material conformity requires exact alloy specification and supporting certificates. A titanium machine frame and an invasive tattoo needle are distinct materials and exposure paths.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/items/138077746"],"citation":["https://www.astm.org/f0136-13r21.html","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/Titanium","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10780041/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9389932/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31451117/"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-ENGINEERING-003","name":"Needle stability and long-term claims","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_RESEARCH_WITH_MEASUREMENT_PENDING","description":"Published technical subjects: machining tolerance, runout, motor speed changes, needle penetration, skin response, pigment deposition, line visibility and long-term appearance. Comparative numerical claims require measurement methodology, biological evidence and longitudinal observation as applicable.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/25/185755"],"citation":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31451117/"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-RESEARCH-001","name":"Cover-up and pigment interaction","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_METHOD_AND_RESEARCH","description":"Published work discusses existing tattoos, pigment density, skin condition, scar tissue, blackout and blackwork integration, white-line techniques and optical concealment. Visual covering and physical pigment removal are different processes; proposed granulation and pigment interaction models retain their research status.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/17/013900","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/07/11/212320"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-TRAINING-001","name":"International tattoo hygiene training","creativeWorkStatus":"FIRST_PERSON_TRAINING_DECLARATION","description":"The practitioner describes European hygiene learning, bloodborne pathogen prevention, infection control and contaminated waste handling, with German Bavarian Custom Irons practice context. Course identity, dates, hours, provider and certificates are separate documents pending linkage.","isBasedOn":["https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/12/185252","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/blog/2025/08/23/121641","https://www.bavariancustomirons.jp/about"],"citation":["https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tattooing-and-body-piercing-infection-prevention-and-control"]},{"@type":"CreativeWork","identifier":"L-MEDICAL-001","name":"Medical institution reference relationships","creativeWorkStatus":"PUBLISHED_REFERENCES_SCOPE_PENDING","description":"Official publications mention https://yok